msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up your workflow code to write logs, report errors to your local notebook, and save partial work when a job is canceled. To read these outputs from your local notebook, see [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Sediakan kod aliran kerja anda untuk menulis log, melaporkan ralat ke notebook tempatan anda, dan menyimpan kerja separa apabila job dibatalkan. Untuk membaca output ini daripada notebook tempatan anda, lihat [Jalankan aliran kerja terurus](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| In the workflow | In your local notebook |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Write with a logger from the `logging` module, or call `print()`. | `job.logs()` returns the lines. |\n"
"| Raise an exception, or exit with a nonzero code. | `job.status()` returns `ERROR`, and `job.logs()` shows the traceback. |\n"
"| Call `send_error()`. | `job.error_message()` and `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` return the code, message, and details. |\n"
"| Call `save_result()` in a `SIGTERM` handler. | `job.result()` returns the partial result of a canceled job. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Dalam aliran kerja | Dalam notebook tempatan anda |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Tulis dengan logger daripada modul `logging`, atau panggil `print()`. | `job.logs()` mengembalikan baris tersebut. |\n"
"| Timbulkan pengecualian, atau keluar dengan kod bukan sifar. | `job.status()` mengembalikan `ERROR`, dan `job.logs()` menunjukkan traceback. |\n"
"| Panggil `send_error()`. | `job.error_message()` dan `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` mengembalikan kod, mesej dan butiran. |\n"
"| Panggil `save_result()` dalam pengendali `SIGTERM`. | `job.result()` mengembalikan hasil separa bagi job yang dibatalkan. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs {#write-logs}"
msgstr "Tulis log {#write-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. Read the logs with `job.logs()` while the job runs or after it ends.\n"
msgstr "Apa-apa sahaja yang ditulis oleh aliran kerja ke output standard atau ralat standard masuk ke log job. Baca log dengan `job.logs()` semasa job berjalan atau selepas ia tamat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up a logger {#set-up-a-logger}"
msgstr "Sediakan logger {#set-up-a-logger}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the `logging` module from the Python standard library. `logging.basicConfig()` writes to standard error, which reaches the logs without delay. The format in the following example adds a timestamp to each line:\n"
msgstr "Gunakan modul `logging` daripada pustaka standard Python. `logging.basicConfig()` menulis ke ralat standard, yang sampai ke log tanpa kelewatan. Format dalam contoh berikut menambah cap masa pada setiap baris:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`level=logging.WARNING` hides `INFO` messages from other packages, and `logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` keeps `INFO` messages for your own logger. `qiskit_ibm_runtime` sets its own level with the `QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL` environment variable.\n"
msgstr "`level=logging.WARNING` menyembunyikan mesej `INFO` daripada pakej lain, dan `logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` mengekalkan mesej `INFO` untuk logger anda sendiri. `qiskit_ibm_runtime` menetapkan tahapnya sendiri dengan pemboleh ubah persekitaran `QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`print()` also reaches the logs, but standard output is buffered, so printed lines might not appear until the job ends. If you use `print()`, pass `flush=True`.\n"
msgstr "`print()` juga sampai ke log, tetapi output standard dibuffer, jadi baris yang dicetak mungkin tidak muncul sehingga job tamat. Jika anda menggunakan `print()`, hantar `flush=True`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: get_logger() from qiskit_serverless adds a [PUBLIC] prefix that Functions uses to split provider and user logs for Catalog Functions; custom workflow logs strip it. Tested with 0.37.0: its lines have no timestamp, and logger.exception() and exc_info=True drop the traceback (PrefixFormatter builds new records with exc_info=None). Confirm whether to recommend the standard logging module for custom workflows, or to fix get_logger(). */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the log level for each run {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"
msgstr "Tetapkan tahap log untuk setiap larian {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To debug one run without changing the code, pass the log level as an argument:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menyahpepijat satu larian tanpa mengubah kod, hantar tahap log sebagai argumen:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, set the level of your logger from the argument:\n"
msgstr "Untuk membolehkan ini, tetapkan tahap logger anda daripada argumen:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow has an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), declare `log_level` in it, for example as `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\"]}`.\n"
msgstr "Jika aliran kerja mempunyai [skema argumen](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), isytiharkan `log_level` di dalamnya, contohnya sebagai `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\"]}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: decide what to log {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"
msgstr "Amalan terbaik: tentukan apa yang perlu dilog {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Log enough to reconstruct a run from its logs:\n"
msgstr "Log secukupnya untuk membina semula larian daripada lognya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**At the start, log what the run received.** Log the backend name, the number of circuits, and the other settings that change between runs.\n"
msgstr "**Pada permulaan, log apa yang diterima larian.** Log nama backend, bilangan litar, dan tetapan lain yang berubah antara larian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log the start and end of each stage.** Use fixed messages that you can search for.\n"
msgstr "**Log permulaan dan penghujung setiap peringkat.** Gunakan mesej tetap yang boleh anda cari.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log iterations at a fixed interval.** For example, log a line such as `iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` every 10 iterations, instead of every iteration.\n"
msgstr "**Log lelaran pada sela tetap.** Contohnya, log baris seperti `iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` setiap 10 lelaran, bukannya setiap lelaran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log exceptions with `logger.exception()` inside an `except` block.** The line includes the full traceback, even if the workflow recovers from the error.\n"
msgstr "**Log pengecualian dengan `logger.exception()` di dalam blok `except`.** Baris itu merangkumi traceback penuh, walaupun aliran kerja pulih daripada ralat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Turn off progress bars.** The logs store each refresh of a progress bar, such as one from `tqdm`, as a separate line. Pass `disable=True` to `tqdm`, or log at an interval instead.\n"
msgstr "**Matikan bar kemajuan.** Log menyimpan setiap muat semula bar kemajuan, seperti daripada `tqdm`, sebagai baris berasingan. Hantar `disable=True` kepada `tqdm`, atau log pada sela masa sebaliknya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Keep the logs small.** Do not log large data, such as every shot. A managed workflow keeps only the newest 50 MB of logs for each job.\n"
msgstr "**Pastikan log kecil.** Jangan log data besar, seperti setiap shot. Aliran kerja terurus hanya menyimpan 50 MB log terbaharu bagi setiap job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Use the words \"error\" and \"exception\" only in messages about failures.** If a failed job did not [report its error](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that include these words.\n"
msgstr "**Gunakan perkataan \"error\" dan \"exception\" hanya dalam mesej tentang kegagalan.** Jika job yang gagal tidak [melaporkan ralatnya](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), pengecualian yang ditimbulkan oleh `job.result()` hanya mengandungi baris log yang memasukkan perkataan ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: report errors with send_error() {#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error}"
msgstr "Amalan terbaik: laporkan ralat dengan send_error() {#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status, and the traceback goes to the logs. A managed workflow does not store the error, even for a `ServerlessError`. `job.error_message()` returns `{}`, and the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that include `error` or `exception`. Checks of argument types and ranges belong in an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), which rejects a bad run before the job starts.\n"
msgstr "Apabila aliran kerja menimbulkan pengecualian, job berakhir dengan status `ERROR`, dan traceback masuk ke log. Aliran kerja terurus tidak menyimpan ralat itu, walaupun untuk `ServerlessError`. `job.error_message()` mengembalikan `{}`, dan pengecualian yang ditimbulkan oleh `job.result()` hanya mengandungi baris log yang memasukkan `error` atau `exception`. Semakan jenis dan julat argumen sepatutnya berada dalam [skema argumen](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), yang menolak larian yang buruk sebelum job bermula.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report every error that stops the workflow with `send_error()`, so that your local notebook gets a short error with a code and details:\n"
msgstr "Laporkan setiap ralat yang menghentikan aliran kerja dengan `send_error()`, supaya notebook tempatan anda mendapat ralat ringkas dengan kod dan butiran:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException` with the same text.\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` menimbulkan `QiskitServerlessException` dengan teks yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, raise `ServerlessError` where the error happens, and wrap the code of your entrypoint in a `try` block that sends any error with `send_error()`. A workflow adds this handler to Catalog Functions, but not to managed workflows:\n"
msgstr "Untuk membolehkan ini, timbulkan `ServerlessError` di tempat ralat berlaku, dan bungkus kod titik masuk anda dalam blok `try` yang menghantar sebarang ralat dengan `send_error()`. Aliran kerja menambah pengendali ini kepada Catalog Functions, tetapi tidak kepada aliran kerja terurus:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Raise the error again.** The final `raise` keeps the traceback in the logs and ends the job with the `ERROR` status.\n"
msgstr "**Timbulkan ralat itu sekali lagi.** `raise` terakhir mengekalkan traceback dalam log dan menamatkan job dengan status `ERROR`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Subclass `ServerlessError` to name a group of errors.** The handler sends the name of the class, such as `InputError`, as the `exception` field.\n"
msgstr "**Jadikan `ServerlessError` subkelas untuk menamakan satu kumpulan ralat.** Pengendali menghantar nama kelas, seperti `InputError`, sebagai medan `exception`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other exceptions also reach the handler.** They get the code `1`, and their `repr()` becomes the message, such as `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"
msgstr "**Pengecualian lain juga sampai ke pengendali.** Ia mendapat kod `1`, dan `repr()` mereka menjadi mesej, seperti `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: custom (user) workflows run their entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py (fleets_runner.py _upload_custom_image_entrypoint). Only provider jobs get the main.tmpl handler, which calls send_error() for an uncaught exception. Should custom jobs get the same handler? Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0: a raised ServerlessError creates no ERROR event, and error_message() returns {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report a problem and continue {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"
msgstr "Laporkan masalah dan teruskan {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`send_error()` does not stop the workflow or change its status, so you can also report problems that the workflow recovers from, such as each circuit that it skips:\n"
msgstr "`send_error()` tidak menghentikan aliran kerja atau mengubah statusnya, jadi anda juga boleh melaporkan masalah yang dipulihkan oleh aliran kerja, seperti setiap litar yang dilangkaunya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns every error that the workflow reported, including the errors of a job that ended with the `DONE` status. See [Find the cause of an error](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-error).\n"
msgstr "`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` mengembalikan setiap ralat yang dilaporkan oleh aliran kerja, termasuk ralat bagi job yang berakhir dengan status `DONE`. Lihat [Cari punca ralat](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-error).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pass numbers and strings in `args`.** `error_message()` shows only the first item of a list.\n"
msgstr "**Hantar nombor dan rentetan dalam `args`.** `error_message()` hanya menunjukkan item pertama dalam senarai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Check the return value.** If a workflow cannot store the error, for example because the code runs outside a job, `send_error()` writes the error to the logs and returns `False`.\n"
msgstr "**Semak nilai pulangan.** Jika aliran kerja tidak dapat menyimpan ralat, contohnya kerana kod berjalan di luar job, `send_error()` menulis ralat ke log dan mengembalikan `False`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm which error codes user workflows should use. Catalog Function codes come from the IBM Quantum error code registry, which might not apply to user workflows. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clean up when a job is canceled {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"
msgstr "Bersihkan apabila job dibatalkan {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint, uploads the final logs, and shuts down the environment. Without a handler, Python stops immediately, and `finally` blocks do not run. The workflow also tries to cancel the QPU jobs and sessions that the workflow started with `get_runtime_service()`. See [Cancel linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Apabila anda membatalkan job, aliran kerja menghantar `SIGTERM` kepada titik masuk anda, memuat naik log akhir, dan menutup persekitaran. Tanpa pengendali, Python berhenti serta-merta, dan blok `finally` tidak dijalankan. Aliran kerja juga cuba membatalkan job dan session QPU yang dimulakan oleh aliran kerja dengan `get_runtime_service()`. Lihat [Batalkan job QPU yang dipautkan](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep partial work, register a handler for `SIGTERM`. Your local notebook then gets the partial result from a canceled job:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menyimpan kerja separa, daftarkan pengendali untuk `SIGTERM`. Notebook tempatan anda kemudian mendapat hasil separa daripada job yang dibatalkan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, add the handler at the start of your entrypoint:\n"
msgstr "Untuk membolehkan ini, tambahkan pengendali pada permulaan titik masuk anda:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`sys.exit()` in the handler raises `SystemExit` in the code that is running, so `finally` blocks run before the script ends. The job still ends with the `CANCELED` status.\n"
msgstr "`sys.exit()` dalam pengendali menimbulkan `SystemExit` dalam kod yang sedang berjalan, jadi blok `finally` dijalankan sebelum skrip tamat. Job masih berakhir dengan status `CANCELED`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the handler short, because the workflow shuts down the environment soon after `SIGTERM`. For long runs, also save checkpoints, so that a later run can resume after a job fails or reaches the 24-hour limit. See [Best practice: checkpoint long jobs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Pastikan pengendali ringkas, kerana aliran kerja menutup persekitaran sejurus selepas `SIGTERM`. Untuk larian yang panjang, simpan juga titik semak, supaya larian kemudian boleh disambung semula selepas kerja gagal atau mencapai had 24 jam. Lihat [Amalan terbaik: titik semak untuk kerja panjang](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm the time between SIGTERM and shutdown. The cancel is a Code Engine hard stop (fleets/handler.py cancel_job, cancel_processing_tasks=True), and the repo sets no grace period. Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0, the real fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py, and docker stop: the handler runs, save_result() writes the result, and result() on a CANCELED job returns it (the result endpoint does not check the status). Confirm on Fleets that a result written in the handler reaches storage before the hard stop. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah seterusnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to start a job and read its status, logs, and result.\n"
"- [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) to save checkpoints that a later run can resume from.\n"
"- [Choose a compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) to run your workflow with more CPU, memory, or GPU resources.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Cadangan\">\n"
"- [Jalankan aliran kerja terurus](/guides/run-managed-workflow) untuk memulakan kerja dan membaca status, log dan hasilnya.\n"
"- [Urus fail merentas larian](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) untuk menyimpan titik semak yang boleh disambung semula oleh larian kemudian.\n"
"- [Pilih profil pengkomputeran](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) untuk menjalankan aliran kerja anda dengan lebih banyak sumber CPU, memori atau GPU.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
